@* HOUSE STYLE FOR THE LEGAL PAGES (rewritten 2026-09-22, user direction: "the tone in the
   document is not authoritative", and "the short version" reads as generic AI copy).

   This page and /terms state what SACC Software Limited does. They do not apologise for it,
   hedge it, or compare it to what anybody else writes. Four rules, and they are why the
   wording below reads as it does:

     1. DECLARE, NEVER TRY. "This policy sets out", not "this policy tries to be honest".
        A document that hedges its own authority has none.
     2. NO COMPARISONS AND NO ASIDES. Earlier drafts said the policy would not "blur it the
        way most privacy pages do" and would not "bury it in a blog post six months later".
        Both are jabs at other companies. They make a legal document sound like a blog.
     3. FULL FORMS, NOT CONTRACTIONS. "do not", "will not", "cannot". This is the single
        largest change here, and the one that carries the register on its own.
     4. NO FORMAT LABELS. "The short version:" names the shape of a paragraph rather than its
        subject. The callout below names what it actually answers.

   What does NOT change: plain English, short sentences, and the concrete numbers — 730 days,
   104 days, 60/30/14, the Tax Procedures Code. Authority here comes from being specific, not
   from sounding like a contract. Every factual claim in this file is load-bearing; reword it
   freely, but do not soften a commitment or drop a figure. *@

